6. Turn today’s frustration into an actual first move

For your television, the immediate objective is to get it working without automatically buying another tier. Verify active streams across the household and account access first; a fourth concurrent stream is enough to trigger the standard-plan limit.

For digital ownership, start comparing games by whether they require online authentication, support meaningful offline play, offer transferable physical editions, and provide credible long-term access. Don’t assume that a physical disc guarantees independence from online services, either.

For broader consumer protection, ReportFraud.ftc.gov⁠￼ accepts reports about suspected deceptive business practices. The FTC also uses aggregated complaints to spot patterns and inform investigations.

One important regulatory distinction: the FTC’s nationwide 2024 click-to-cancel rule was vacated by a federal appeals court in July 2025, though other federal and state consumer-protection laws can still apply.

Here’s where I’d ultimately steer Pantheon:

Don’t build a machine that simply tells people which corporations to hate. Build one that shows people where their money goes, what rights they’re surrendering, how the system keeps them dependent, and exactly what alternatives give them leverage.

Then apply comparative morphology to identify the same mechanism appearing in entirely different industries.

That becomes useful to ordinary families, business owners, and consumers—not just us.

And perhaps the strongest countermeasure is creating businesses that prove customers don’t have to be treated as captive revenue streams for a company to thrive.

Let the companies compete for people’s loyalty by earning it again.